     "why": "Capture's stopped tempo search scores each candidate tempo with logf (seq_capture.c); a last-bit difference between glibc's logf and musl's could reorder near-tied candidates and so the take. Identical to static musl and to fm1-render.js.",
     "cmd": "seq/capture-stopped-capsel.verbs", "fx": [], "seconds": 3.5},
    {"name": "seq-panel-play-stop", "engine": "macro", "params": ["Model=2"], "lab": true,
     "why": "The panel drives the sequencer (docs/15 S3, the lab switch on): the module presses the buttons and turns the encoders; the render legs replay the commands and knob turns the native harness logged (--log-cmds and its .args sidecar), so this is also two-step parity.",
     "cmd": "seq/panel-play-stop.verbs", "panel": "seq/panel-play-stop.panel",
     "fx": [["plate", ["Mix=0.25"]]], "seconds": 2.2},
    {"name": "seq-panel-step-entry", "engine": "macro", "params": ["Model=4"], "lab": true,
     "why": "Step entry from the panel (docs/15 S4, the lab switch on): taps with a chord from MIDI IN, a probability, a condition and an invert on the Step pages, a second bar, a nudge, a pitch added with SHIFT and a step cleared with a SHIFT tap, then two passes of the two-bar clip. The render legs replay what the native harness logged (--log-cmds and its .args sidecar, with the MIDI IN notes); the module presses the same keys and buttons and plays the same notes.",
     "cmd": "seq/panel-step-entry.verbs", "panel": "seq/panel-step-entry.panel",
     "fx": [["plate", ["Mix=0.25"]]], "seconds": 6.0},
    {"name": "seq-panel-record", "engine": "macro", "params": ["Model=4"], "lab": true,
     "why": "Record and Capture from the panel (docs/15 S5, the lab switch on): REC with a bar's count-in and two keys recorded into the take, step record with a chord tied over two steps, a rest and a note at MIDI IN, then three keys captured while playing (SHIFT + REC). The keys' notes reach the sequencer as live input; the render legs replay them as the `non` and `nof` ops the native harness logged, with the keys' notes in its .args sidecar.",
     "cmd": "seq/panel-record.verbs", "panel": "seq/panel-record.panel",
     "fx": [["plate", ["Mix=0.25"]]], "seconds": 6.0},
    {"name": "seq-panel-capture-stopped", "engine": "shapes", "params": ["Shape=28"], "lab": true,
     "libm_sensitive": true,
     "why": "A stopped Capture from the panel (docs/15 S5): six keys, then SHIFT + REC; the core reads the tempo, starts the transport and opens its picker, SELECT takes another tempo and a key closes it. The tempo search scores candidates with logf (seq_capture.c), as seq-capture-stopped-capsel; identical to static musl and to fm1-render.js.",
     "cmd": "seq/panel-capture-stopped.verbs", "panel": "seq/panel-capture-stopped.panel",
     "fx": [], "seconds": 5.0},
